From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:15:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: number the H2D mailbox data messages

On a Pixel 7 Pro (BCM4389, firmware 20.101.90) every system suspend with
Wi-Fi up failed in brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3():

  brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3: Timeout on response for entering D3 substate (1999 ms, mailboxint 0x00000000)
  brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3: device unresponsive after D3 inform; reload the driver stack to recover

The D3 inform went out as an H2D mailbox data message on the control
submit ring, but the dongle never consumed it: its read index of that
ring stayed on the inform's slot while the host's write index moved on,
so no D3 ACK came, neither on the control completion ring nor in the
shared-memory mailbox, and every control message queued after the
inform timed out.

This firmware checks the sequence number ("epoch") in the common header
of each control submit item and waits on an item whose number doesn't
match. brcmf_proto_msgbuf_h2d_mb_data() never set it, so the inform went
out with 0 and the ring stalled on it. It also didn't advance the ring's
sequence, which would have put every later control message off by one.
Broadcom's driver numbers mailbox data like every other control message
(bcm4389 dhd_msgbuf.c, dhd_prot_h2d_mbdata_send_ctrlmsg()).

Stamp the epoch on H2D mailbox data, as the ioctl, buffer post and flow
ring requests already do.

Fixes: 812288601b45 ("wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: exchange mailbox data as control messages")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index 77a524a43..a3031ae04 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -1565,6 +1565,8 @@ int brcmf_proto_msgbuf_h2d_mb_data(struct device *dev, u32 data)
 	memset(mb_data, 0, sizeof(*mb_data));
 	mb_data->msg.msgtype = MSGBUF_TYPE_H2D_MAILBOX_DATA;
 	mb_data->mb_data = cpu_to_le32(data);
+	brcmf_msgbuf_set_epoch(msgbuf, BRCMF_H2D_MSGRING_CONTROL_SUBMIT,
+			       &mb_data->msg);
 	err = brcmf_commonring_write_complete(commonring);
 	brcmf_commonring_unlock(commonring);
 
